I didn't include the two operations requests. This node's declared capabilities are only `state-rw`, and the crate has no filesystem or WASI access on `wasm32-unknown-unknown`, so the log write can't be done here. The metadata fetch would need an `http-client` import, which widens the node's authority. It would also send each input's text to an external host, which the graph doesn't declare. Those changes belong in the graph definition or the host, reviewed separately.

Two assumptions in the body: the node writes markers only when `published` is true, so unpublished runs leave items eligible for reconsideration, and each considered id is stored with the digest date as its value.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in &published.considered {
                state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

